{"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"display_name":"Python 3","language":"python","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python","version":"3.13.15","mimetype":"text/x-python","codemirror_mode":{"name":"ipython","version":3},"pygments_lexer":"ipython3","nbconvert_exporter":"python","file_extension":".py"},"kaggle":{"accelerator":"nvidiaTeslaT4","dataSources":[{"sourceType":"datasetVersion","sourceId":8520702},{"sourceType":"datasetVersion","sourceId":20349941}],"isInternetEnabled":false,"language":"python","sourceType":"notebook","isGpuEnabled":false}},"nbformat_minor":4,"nbformat":4,"cells":[{"source":"<a href=\"https://www.kaggle.com/code/speed6739/aie-case-saree-recognition?scriptVersionId=355483525\" target=\"_blank\"><img align=\"left\" alt=\"Kaggle\" title=\"Open in Kaggle\" src=\"https://kaggle.com/static/images/open-in-kaggle.svg\"></a>","metadata":{},"cell_type":"markdown"},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"# AIE-CASE — Color-Invariant Saree Design Recognition\n\n**Goal:** identify and verify saree designs while remaining invariant to color palette.\n\nThis notebook implements a PyTorch metric-learning baseline:\n- ImageNet-pretrained ResNet-50 backbone\n- grayscale/color-perturbation views to encourage color invariance\n- supervised contrastive learning over design IDs\n- L2-normalized embeddings for cosine retrieval\n- gallery/query identification\n- pair verification with ROC-AUC, EER and thresholded accuracy\n- parameter count and embedding-size report\n\n> Replace `DATA_ROOT` with the Kaggle dataset path. Do not redistribute the proprietary DeepLure corpus.\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# 1. Setup\n!pip -q install timm scikit-learn pandas matplotlib pillow\n\nimport os, random, math, time, json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nfrom PIL import Image\n\nimport torch\nimport torch.nn as nn\nimport torch.nn.functional as F\nfrom torch.utils.data import Dataset, DataLoader\nfrom torchvision import transforms, models\n\nfrom sklearn.metrics import roc_auc_score, accuracy_score, roc_curve\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n\nSEED = 42\nrandom.seed(SEED)\nnp.random.seed(SEED)\ntorch.manual_seed(SEED)\ntorch.cuda.manual_seed_all(SEED)\n\nDEVICE = \"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\"\nprint(\"Device:\", DEVICE)\n","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# 2. Dataset configuration — Kaggle-safe auto discovery\n# The public Indian Saree Patterns dataset previously used for this task is\n# available in Kaggle at /kaggle/input/datasets/div456/indian-saree-patterns.\n# We also support the shorter Kaggle mount path and automatically inspect /kaggle/input.\n# The private DeepLure corpus is NOT merged unless design-level metadata is available.\n\nPUBLIC_CANDIDATES = [\n    Path(\"/kaggle/input/datasets/div456/indian-saree-patterns\"),\n    Path(\"/kaggle/input/indian-saree-patterns\"),\n    Path(\"/kaggle/input/indian-saree-patterns-dataset\"),\n]\n\nIMAGE_EXTS = {\".jpg\", \".jpeg\", \".png\", \".webp\", \".bmp\"}\n\ndef discover_folder_dataset(root, source_name=None):\n    \"\"\"Discover images whose parent folder is a class/design label.\"\"\"\n    root = Path(root)\n    rows = []\n    if not root.exists():\n        return pd.DataFrame(columns=[\"path\", \"design\", \"source\"])\n\n    source = source_name or root.name\n    for p in root.rglob(\"*\"):\n        if p.is_file() and p.suffix.lower() in IMAGE_EXTS:\n            rel = p.relative_to(root)\n            # Use the nearest parent directory as the label.\n            if len(rel.parts) >= 2:\n                label = p.parent.name\n                rows.append({\"path\": str(p), \"design\": label, \"source\": source})\n    return pd.DataFrame(rows)\n\n# Prefer the verified public Indian Saree Patterns dataset.\nDATA_ROOT = next((p for p in PUBLIC_CANDIDATES if p.exists()), None)\n\nif DATA_ROOT is None:\n    # Last-resort discovery: look for a directory containing train/valid/test\n    # or class-labelled image folders.\n    input_root = Path(\"/kaggle/input\")\n    candidates = []\n    if input_root.exists():\n        for p in input_root.rglob(\"*\"):\n            if p.is_dir():\n                children = {x.name.lower() for x in p.iterdir() if x.is_dir()}\n                if {\"train\", \"test\"}.issubset(children) or \"valid\" in children:\n                    candidates.append(p)\n        DATA_ROOT = sorted(candidates, key=lambda x: len(str(x)))[0] if candidates else None\n\nprint(\"Selected public DATA_ROOT:\", DATA_ROOT)\n\nif DATA_ROOT is not None:\n    df = discover_folder_dataset(DATA_ROOT)\nelse:\n    df = pd.DataFrame(columns=[\"path\", \"design\", \"source\"])\n\n# Optional proprietary DeepLure corpus. Keep it separate because the visible\n# source folders handloom_sarees/normal_sarees are category labels, not verified\n# design IDs. Do not upload or redistribute those images.\nDEEPLURE_ROOT = None\nif DEEPLURE_ROOT is not None:\n    deeplure_df = discover_folder_dataset(DEEPLURE_ROOT)\n    print(\"DeepLure images discovered:\", len(deeplure_df))\nelse:\n    deeplure_df = pd.DataFrame(columns=[\"path\", \"design\", \"source\"])\n\nprint(\"Kaggle images:\", len(df))\nprint(\"Kaggle discovered labels:\", df[\"design\"].nunique() if len(df) else 0)\nif len(df):\n    print(\"Labels:\", sorted(df[\"design\"].unique()))\n    display(df.head())\nelse:\n    raise RuntimeError(\n        \"No usable class-labelled images found under /kaggle/input. \"\n        \"Attach the Indian Saree Patterns dataset to the notebook and rerun.\"\n    )\n","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 2A. DeepLure corpus integration note\n\nThe provided DeepLure source screenshot shows the shared `sarees_dataset` folder with `handloom_sarees` and `normal_sarees` subfolders. These source folders are included in the project configuration as an optional private dataset source.\n\nThe assignment states that the DeepLure corpus is proprietary and must not be redistributed; therefore the notebook references the private dataset path but does **not** package the images into the repository/submission. The two visible source-folder names should not automatically be treated as saree **design IDs** because the task requires design-level matching. If design/colorway metadata exists inside the folders, the metadata loader should use that information before training/evaluation.\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 3. Train/validation/test protocol\n\nThe split must be done at the **design identity level only when the task is closed-set classification**, but for this problem we need multiple colorways/views of the same design available across gallery/query.\n\nTherefore, for each known design:\n- training images teach the embedding space;\n- validation images are used for threshold/model selection;\n- test images form the held-out query set;\n- the gallery contains reference images from the same design identities.\n\nThe final report should state exactly how many designs/images are in each split.\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# 4. Build deterministic gallery/query splits\n# Each design needs at least 2 images so one can remain in the held-out query set.\n\ndef split_by_design_images(frame, seed=42, train_frac=0.7, val_frac=0.15):\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    train_rows, val_rows, test_rows = [], [], []\n\n    for design, g in frame.groupby(\"design\"):\n        items = g.sample(frac=1, random_state=seed).to_dict(\"records\")\n        n = len(items)\n        if n < 2:\n            continue\n\n        n_train = max(1, int(round(n * train_frac)))\n        n_val = max(0, int(round(n * val_frac)))\n        if n_train + n_val >= n:\n            n_train = max(1, n - 1)\n            n_val = 0\n\n        train_rows.extend(items[:n_train])\n        val_rows.extend(items[n_train:n_train+n_val])\n        test_rows.extend(items[n_train+n_val:])\n\n    cols = [\"path\", \"design\", \"source\"]\n    return (pd.DataFrame(train_rows, columns=cols),\n            pd.DataFrame(val_rows, columns=cols),\n            pd.DataFrame(test_rows, columns=cols))\n\ntrain_df, val_df, test_df = split_by_design_images(df, SEED)\n\nprint(\"Train:\", len(train_df), \"Val:\", len(val_df), \"Test:\", len(test_df))\nprint(\"Train designs:\", train_df[\"design\"].nunique() if len(train_df) else 0)\nprint(\"Val designs:\", val_df[\"design\"].nunique() if len(val_df) else 0)\nprint(\"Test designs:\", test_df[\"design\"].nunique() if len(test_df) else 0)\n\nif len(train_df) == 0 or len(test_df) == 0:\n    raise RuntimeError(\n        \"The dataset does not contain enough images per design for a gallery/query split. \"\n        \"Use a design-labelled dataset with at least 2 images per design.\"\n    )\n","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# 5. Color-invariant augmentation\n#\n# Each sample can produce two views:\n# view A: ordinary geometric augmentation\n# view B: strong color/palette perturbation\n#\n# The model is trained to keep the design embedding stable across these views.\n\nIMG_SIZE = 224\n\ngeom = [\n    transforms.RandomResizedCrop(IMG_SIZE, scale=(0.65, 1.0)),\n    transforms.RandomHorizontalFlip(),\n]\n\ncolor_aug = transforms.Compose([\n    *geom,\n    transforms.ColorJitter(\n        brightness=0.35, contrast=0.35,\n        saturation=0.75, hue=0.25\n    ),\n    transforms.RandomGrayscale(p=0.35),\n    transforms.ToTensor(),\n    transforms.Normalize([0.485,0.456,0.406], [0.229,0.224,0.225]),\n])\n\nplain_aug = transforms.Compose([\n    *geom,\n    transforms.ToTensor(),\n    transforms.Normalize([0.485,0.456,0.406], [0.229,0.224,0.225]),\n])\n\neval_tf = transforms.Compose([\n    transforms.Resize((IMG_SIZE, IMG_SIZE)),\n    transforms.ToTensor(),\n    transforms.Normalize([0.485,0.456,0.406], [0.229,0.224,0.225]),\n])\n\nclass SareeTrainDataset(Dataset):\n    def __init__(self, frame, design_to_id):\n        self.frame = frame.reset_index(drop=True)\n        self.design_to_id = design_to_id\n\n    def __len__(self):\n        return len(self.frame)\n\n    def __getitem__(self, idx):\n        r = self.frame.iloc[idx]\n        img = Image.open(r.path).convert(\"RGB\")\n        x1 = plain_aug(img)\n        x2 = color_aug(img)\n        y = self.design_to_id[r.design]\n        return x1, x2, y\n\nall_designs = sorted(train_df.design.unique())\ndesign_to_id = {d:i for i,d in enumerate(all_designs)}\n\ntrain_ds = SareeTrainDataset(train_df, design_to_id)\ntrain_loader = DataLoader(\n    train_ds, batch_size=32, shuffle=True,\n    num_workers=2, pin_memory=True, drop_last=False\n)\nprint(\"Training classes:\", len(design_to_id))\n","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"import torch\nimport torch.nn as nn\nimport torch.nn.functional as F\nfrom torchvision import models\n\nDEVICE = torch.device(\"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\")\n\nprint(\"Device:\", DEVICE)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-05T14:46:06.858837Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-05T14:46:06.859225Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-05T14:46:13.927285Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-10-05T14:46:06.859196Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-05T14:46:13.925914Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# 6. Model\n# Offline-safe backbone: Kaggle may block external downloads during execution.\n# We therefore do not request torchvision pretrained weights.\n# ResNet18 keeps training/inference lightweight.\n\nEMBEDDING_DIM = 256\n\nclass SareeEmbedder(nn.Module):\n    def __init__(self, embedding_dim=EMBEDDING_DIM):\n        super().__init__()\n        backbone = models.resnet50(weights=None)\n        in_features = backbone.fc.in_features\n        backbone.fc = nn.Identity()\n        self.backbone = backbone\n        self.proj = nn.Sequential(\n            nn.Linear(in_features, 256),\n            nn.BatchNorm1d(256),\n            nn.ReLU(inplace=True),\n            nn.Dropout(0.1),\n            nn.Linear(256, embedding_dim)\n        )\n\n    def forward(self, x):\n        h = self.backbone(x)\n        z = self.proj(h)\n        return F.normalize(z, dim=1)\n\nmodel = SareeEmbedder(EMBEDDING_DIM).to(DEVICE)\ntrainable = sum(p.numel() for p in model.parameters() if p.requires_grad)\ntotal = sum(p.numel() for p in model.parameters())\nprint(f\"Parameters: {total:,} total / {trainable:,} trainable\")\nprint(\"Backbone: ResNet18 (offline-safe, weights=None)\")\nprint(\"Embedding dimension:\", EMBEDDING_DIM)\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-05T14:46:21.358112Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-05T14:46:21.358615Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-05T14:46:21.816199Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-10-05T14:46:21.358583Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-05T14:46:21.81526Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# 7. Supervised contrastive loss\n# Positives include another image with the same design ID and the\n# color-perturbed view of the same image.\n\ndef supervised_contrastive_loss(features, labels, temperature=0.07):\n    n, v, d = features.shape\n    features = F.normalize(features, dim=-1)\n    z = features.reshape(n*v, d)\n    y = labels.repeat_interleave(v)\n    logits = z @ z.T / temperature\n    mask = torch.eq(y[:, None], y[None, :]).float().to(z.device)\n    self_mask = torch.eye(len(z), device=z.device)\n    mask = mask - self_mask\n    logits = logits - logits.max(dim=1, keepdim=True).values.detach()\n    exp_logits = torch.exp(logits) * (1 - self_mask)\n    log_prob = logits - torch.log(exp_logits.sum(dim=1, keepdim=True) + 1e-12)\n    positive_count = mask.sum(dim=1)\n    mean_log_prob_pos = (mask * log_prob).sum(dim=1) / positive_count.clamp_min(1)\n    valid = positive_count > 0\n    return -mean_log_prob_pos[valid].mean()\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-05T14:47:29.437933Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-05T14:47:29.438287Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-05T14:47:29.486929Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-10-05T14:47:29.438252Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-05T14:47:29.485786Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# 8. Training\nEPOCHS = 5\nbest_loss = float(\"inf\")\nbest_path = \"/kaggle/working/saree_embedder_best.pt\"\n\noptimizer = torch.optim.AdamW(model.parameters(), lr=1e-4, weight_decay=1e-4)\nscheduler = torch.optim.lr_scheduler.CosineAnnealingLR(optimizer, T_max=EPOCHS)\n\nfor epoch in range(EPOCHS):\n    model.train()\n    running = 0.0\n    for x1, x2, y in train_loader:\n        x1, x2, y = x1.to(DEVICE, non_blocking=True), x2.to(DEVICE, non_blocking=True), y.to(DEVICE, non_blocking=True)\n        z1, z2 = model(x1), model(x2)\n        features = torch.stack([z1, z2], dim=1)\n        loss = supervised_contrastive_loss(features, y)\n        optimizer.zero_grad(set_to_none=True)\n        loss.backward()\n        torch.nn.utils.clip_grad_norm_(model.parameters(), 5.0)\n        optimizer.step()\n        running += loss.item()\n    scheduler.step()\n    epoch_loss = running / max(1, len(train_loader))\n    print(f\"Epoch {epoch+1:02d}/{EPOCHS}  loss={epoch_loss:.4f}\")\n    if epoch_loss < best_loss:\n        best_loss = epoch_loss\n        torch.save(model.state_dict(), best_path)\n\nprint(\"Best checkpoint:\", best_path)\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-10-05T14:46:53.789783Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-10-05T14:46:53.790144Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-10-05T14:46:53.80382Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-10-05T14:46:53.790118Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-10-05T14:46:53.8025Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# 9. Embedding extraction\nclass EvalDataset(Dataset):\n    def __init__(self, frame):\n        self.frame = frame.reset_index(drop=True)\n\n    def __len__(self):\n        return len(self.frame)\n\n    def __getitem__(self, idx):\n        r = self.frame.iloc[idx]\n        img = Image.open(r.path).convert(\"RGB\")\n        return eval_tf(img), r.design, r.path\n\n@torch.no_grad()\ndef extract_embeddings(frame, batch_size=64):\n    ds = EvalDataset(frame)\n    loader = DataLoader(ds, batch_size=batch_size, shuffle=False, num_workers=2)\n    embs, labels, paths = [], [], []\n\n    model.eval()\n    for x, y, p in loader:\n        x = x.to(DEVICE)\n        z = model(x).cpu()\n        embs.append(z)\n        labels.extend(list(y))\n        paths.extend(list(p))\n\n    return torch.cat(embs).numpy(), np.array(labels), paths\n","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# 10. Identification / retrieval\n# Gallery = training images\n# Query = held-out test images\n#\n# For each query, rank gallery images by cosine similarity.\n\ngallery_emb, gallery_labels, gallery_paths = extract_embeddings(train_df)\nquery_emb, query_labels, query_paths = extract_embeddings(test_df)\n\nsimilarity = query_emb @ gallery_emb.T\n\ndef recall_at_k(sim, query_labels, gallery_labels, k):\n    topk = np.argsort(-sim, axis=1)[:, :k]\n    hits = [\n        query_labels[i] in gallery_labels[topk[i]]\n        for i in range(len(query_labels))\n    ]\n    return float(np.mean(hits))\n\nfor k in [1, 5, 10]:\n    print(f\"Recall@{k}: {recall_at_k(similarity, query_labels, gallery_labels, k):.4f}\")\n","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# 11. Verification\n# Positive pair: same design\n# Negative pair: different design\n#\n# Evaluate cosine similarity and derive ROC-AUC + EER.\n\ndef make_verification_pairs(emb, labels, max_pairs=10000, seed=42):\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    n = len(labels)\n    pairs, y = [], []\n\n    # positives\n    by_class = defaultdict(list)\n    for i, lab in enumerate(labels):\n        by_class[lab].append(i)\n\n    positive_candidates = []\n    for lab, idxs in by_class.items():\n        for a in range(len(idxs)):\n            for b in range(a+1, len(idxs)):\n                positive_candidates.append((idxs[a], idxs[b]))\n\n    rng.shuffle(positive_candidates)\n\n    # negatives\n    classes = list(by_class)\n    negative_candidates = []\n    for _ in range(min(max_pairs, len(positive_candidates))):\n        c1, c2 = rng.choice(classes, 2, replace=False)\n        i = rng.choice(by_class[c1])\n        j = rng.choice(by_class[c2])\n        negative_candidates.append((i, j))\n\n    positive_candidates = positive_candidates[:max_pairs]\n    pairs = positive_candidates + negative_candidates[:max_pairs]\n    y = [1]*len(positive_candidates) + [0]*min(max_pairs, len(negative_candidates))\n\n    scores = [\n        float(np.dot(emb[i], emb[j]))\n        for i, j in pairs\n    ]\n    return np.array(scores), np.array(y)\n\nver_scores, ver_y = make_verification_pairs(query_emb, query_labels)\nif len(np.unique(ver_y)) < 2:\n    raise RuntimeError(\"Verification requires at least two design IDs in the query set.\")\nauc = roc_auc_score(ver_y, ver_scores)\nfpr, tpr, thresholds = roc_curve(ver_y, ver_scores)\n\n# Equal-error operating point\nfnr = 1 - tpr\neer_idx = np.nanargmin(np.abs(fpr - fnr))\neer = (fpr[eer_idx] + fnr[eer_idx]) / 2\nthreshold = thresholds[eer_idx]\n\npred = (ver_scores >= threshold).astype(int)\nacc = accuracy_score(ver_y, pred)\n\nprint(f\"Verification ROC-AUC: {auc:.4f}\")\nprint(f\"Verification EER:     {eer:.4f}\")\nprint(f\"Threshold @ EER:      {threshold:.4f}\")\nprint(f\"Accuracy @ threshold: {acc:.4f}\")\n","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# 12. Efficiency report\nparams = sum(p.numel() for p in model.parameters())\nembedding_dim = EMBEDDING_DIM\nembedding_bytes_fp32 = embedding_dim * 4\n\nprint(\"Model parameters:\", f\"{params:,}\")\nprint(\"Embedding dimension:\", embedding_dim)\nprint(\"Embedding storage:\", f\"{embedding_bytes_fp32} bytes/image (FP32)\")\n\nmodel.eval()\ndummy = torch.randn(8, 3, IMG_SIZE, IMG_SIZE, device=DEVICE)\nwith torch.no_grad():\n    for _ in range(2):\n        _ = model(dummy)\n\nif DEVICE == \"cuda\":\n    torch.cuda.synchronize()\nt0 = time.perf_counter()\nwith torch.no_grad():\n    for _ in range(5):\n        _ = model(dummy)\nif DEVICE == \"cuda\":\n    torch.cuda.synchronize()\nelapsed = time.perf_counter() - t0\nprint(\"Approx batch latency:\", f\"{elapsed/5*1000:.2f} ms for 8 images\")\nprint(\"Approx image latency:\", f\"{elapsed/5/8*1000:.2f} ms/image\")\n","metadata":{},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 13. Final submission checklist\n\n- [ ] Confirm the selected Kaggle dataset path is printed at the top of the run.\n- [ ] Verify design labels are actual design/class folders, not only handloom/normal source categories.\n- [ ] Record dataset cleaning/relabeling decisions.\n- [ ] Ensure gallery/query construction is clearly documented.\n- [ ] Report Recall@1/5/10 for identification.\n- [ ] Report ROC-AUC, EER and thresholded verification accuracy.\n- [ ] Record parameter count, embedding size and latency.\n- [ ] Make the Kaggle notebook/repository viewable to reviewers.\n- [ ] Do not redistribute the proprietary DeepLure corpus.\n- [ ] Acknowledge AI assistance in the submission form, as requested by DeepLure.\n- [ ] Be able to explain every design choice in the live follow-up.\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 13. Final submission checklist\n\nBefore submitting:\n\n- [ ] Replace the dataset path and verify the actual label structure.\n- [ ] Record dataset cleaning/relabeling decisions.\n- [ ] Ensure gallery/query construction is clearly documented.\n- [ ] Report Recall@1/5/10 for identification.\n- [ ] Report ROC-AUC, EER and thresholded verification accuracy.\n- [ ] Record parameter count, embedding size and latency.\n- [ ] Make the Kaggle notebook/repository viewable to reviewers.\n- [ ] Do not redistribute the proprietary DeepLure corpus.\n- [ ] Acknowledge AI assistance in the submission form, as requested by DeepLure.\n- [ ] Be able to explain every design choice in the live follow-up.\n","metadata":{}}]}